 travel company, provides travel and leisure services and products to residents of under-served cities in the United States. The company offers scheduled air transportation on limited-frequency, nonstop flights between underserved cities and leisure destinations. As of February 1, 2026, it operated a fleet of 106 Airbus A320 series aircraft and 16 Boeing 737 series aircraft. The company also provides air-related services and products in conjunction with air transportation, including larger seats, baggage fees, advance seat assignments, travel protection products, change fees, priority boarding, customer convenience fee, food and beverage purchases on board, and other air-related services, as well as use of its call center for purchases. In addition, it offers third party travel products, such as hotel rooms, rental cars, and travel insurance from a third-party insurer; air transportation services; and charter services on a year-round and ad-hoc basis. Further, the company owns and operates a golf course. Allegiant Travel Company was founded in 1997 and is based in Las Vegas, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gregory Clark Anderson CPA | CEO & Director | Age 43 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $307K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Allegiant Travel Company is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.5B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $75M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -10.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 35% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Allegiant Travel (ALGT) Director Jude Bricker Resigns After Board Role In Deal Closes","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nasdaq-algt/allegiant-travel/news/allegiant-travel-algt-director-jude-bricker-resigns-after-bo","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793960925.549,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Allegiant (ALGT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/allegiant-algt-q3-2026-earnings-160529395.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793894729.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Allegiant Travel (ALGT) Trading At A Premium To Sales?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nasdaq-algt/allegiant-travel/news/is-allegiant-travel-algt-trading-at-a-premium-to-sales","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793867524.258,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Allegiant signals 2026 EPS over $6 as it targets $140M in Sun Country synergies by 2029 (NASDAQ:ALGT)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666254-allegiant-signals-2026-eps-over-6-as-it-targets-140m-in-sun-country-synergies-by-2029","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793867229.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Allegiant Travel Co (ALGT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Record T